u0:U0_0000093 skos:definition "A mandate-bearing accountable agent (human office-holder) that may issue governance Decisions.";
  skos:prefLabel "Accountable Agent" .

u0:U0_0000095 skos:definition "Links an Authority Mandate to its accountable mandate holder.";
  skos:prefLabel "Mandate Holder" .

u0:U0_0000064 skos:definition "Mandate context under which an authority-bearing decision may be exercised. Absence of mandate is meaningful and must not be treated as permission.";
  skos:prefLabel "Authority Mandate" .

u0:U0_0000091 skos:definition "Relates an eligibility state assertion to the anchor it is about, enforcing identity continuity for governed eligibility.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility About Anchor" .

u0:U0_0000081 skos:definition "A governed, explicit scope that constrains what may be claimed, delivered, operated, or defended. Claim scope is not inferred from execution; it exists only when established and maintained under governance decisions.";
  skos:prefLabel "Claim Scope" .

u0:U0_0000088 skos:definition "Relates an eligibility state assertion to the claim scope it governs.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility For Claim Scope" .

u0:U0_0000089 skos:definition "Relates an eligibility state assertion to the governance decision that establishes or revokes eligibility. The decision's enactsTransition must express the eligibility change.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Established By Decision" .

u0:U0_0000066 skos:definition "Controlled transition type enacted by an explicit decision. Transitions are governance-plane semantics and must not be inferred from mechanism execution.";
  skos:prefLabel "Governance State Transition" .

u0:U0_0000072 skos:definition "Governance transition type: eligibility granted.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Granted" .

u0:U0_0000073 skos:definition "Governance transition type: eligibility revoked.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Revoked" .

u0:U0_0000090 skos:definition "Relates an eligibility state assertion to the governance transition type it asserts (e.g., Eligibility Granted or Eligibility Revoked).";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Transition Type" .

u0:U0_0000083 skos:definition "A governance state assertion concerning eligibility for a specific claim scope. It must be explicitly tied to a governance decision and must not be inferred from mechanism execution, evidence presence, confidence, or completion.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility State Assertion" .

u0:U0_0000085 skos:definition "Relates a governed operating asset to the governance decision that explicitly establishes or re-establishes its governed status for a particular scope.";
  skos:prefLabel "Established By Decision" .

u0:U0_0000086 skos:definition "Relates a governed operating asset to the authority mandate context under which it was established. This must be explicit to prevent portability or implicit re-use.";
  skos:prefLabel "Established Under Mandate" .

u0:U0_0000092 skos:definition "Relates a governed operating asset to the anchor it is about, enforcing identity continuity for governed asset status and preventing portable, context-free eligibility claims.";
  skos:prefLabel "Asset About Anchor" .

u0:U0_0000084 skos:definition "Relates a governed operating asset to its explicit claim scope. Claim scope must be explicit and is not inferred from execution.";
  skos:prefLabel "Has Claim Scope" .

u0:U0_0000082 skos:definition "A governed operating asset is an operational asset whose eligibility and claimability are conditional, scoped, and revocable under governance. It is inseparable from its claim scope, decision provenance, and mandate context; it is not a transferable label.";
  skos:prefLabel "Governed Operating Asset" .

u2:U2_0000103 skos:definition "Links an acceptance decision record to the persistent entity (human or institutional) that is the accountable decision maker.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decision Made By" .

u0:U0_0000065 skos:definition "Declared downside exposure scope associated with exercising a mandate or decision. It is descriptive of risk exposure and does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth.";
  skos:prefLabel "Downside Exposure Scope" .

u0:U0_0000070 skos:definition "Relates a decision record to the declared downside exposure scope associated with exercising it. It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth by itself.";
  skos:prefLabel "Declares Downside Exposure" .

u0:U0_0000080 skos:definition "Governance transition type: promotion of a candidate assertion into an accepted construct (admissible-for-use).";
  skos:prefLabel "Accepted Construct Promoted" .

u0:U0_0000071 skos:definition "Relates a decision record to the governance state transition type it enacts. Transitions must not be inferred from mechanism execution.";
  skos:prefLabel "Enacts Transition" .

u2:U2_0000101 skos:definition "Links an acceptance decision record to exactly one candidate assertion that is being decided upon.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decides On Candidate Assertion" .

u2:U2_0000201 skos:definition "Timestamp when the governance decision was made.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decision Time" .

u1:U1_0000013 skos:definition "In layer u1 (Agreement/Proposal (non-authoritative proposals for governance consideration)), 'Profile' is a class used to represent a first-class construct on this layer's semantic axis. It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth.";
  skos:prefLabel "Profile" .

u2:U2_0000102 skos:definition "Links an acceptance decision record to an applicable u1 profile that constrained or structured the decision context.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decision Uses Profile" .

u0:U0_0000062 skos:definition "Objective declared by a decision-maker as the target of an authority-bearing decision. It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth on its own.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decision Objective" .

u0:U0_0000067 skos:definition "Relates a decision record to at least one declared decision objective. It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth by itself.";
  skos:prefLabel "Has Objective" .

u0:U0_0000063 skos:definition "Criterion used to justify why a decision objective is satisfied (or not). It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth on its own.";
  skos:prefLabel "Decision Criterion" .

u0:U0_0000068 skos:definition "Relates a decision record to one or more criteria used to justify the decision. It does not imply acceptance, eligibility, approval, or truth by itself.";
  skos:prefLabel "Justified By Criterion" .

u0:U0_0000069 skos:definition "Relates a decision record to the mandate context under which it was exercised. Absence of mandate is meaningful and must not be treated as permission.";
  skos:prefLabel "Exercised Under Mandate" .

u2:U2_0000001 skos:definition "Explicit governance decision record that authorizes promotion of candidate assertions into accepted-in-system assertions. This record does not assert metaphysical truth and does not imply execution.";
  skos:prefLabel "Acceptance Decision Record" .

u2:U2_0000105 skos:definition "Aboutness link: the accepted-in-system assertion is about exactly one u0 anchor.";
  skos:prefLabel "Accepted Assertion About Anchor" .

u2:U2_0000106 skos:definition "Mandatory provenance link: the accepted-in-system assertion is promoted from exactly one candidate assertion.";
  skos:prefLabel "Promoted From Candidate Assertion" .

u2:U2_0000107 skos:definition "Mandatory justification link: an accepted-in-system assertion must be justified by one or more acceptance decision records.";
  skos:prefLabel "Promotion Justified By Decision" .

u2:U2_0000002 skos:definition "Accepted assertion artefact (accepted-in-system). Represents what the system is willing to treat as admissible for downstream use, under explicit governance decision. Not identical to its referent and not metaphysical truth.";
  skos:prefLabel "Accepted-in-System Assertion" .

u2:U2_0000120 skos:definition "Links an eligibility decision record to the eligibility-target workflow that the decision concerns.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Decision For Workflow" .

u2:U2_0000121 skos:definition "Links an eligibility decision record to the eligibility profile under which the decision was made.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Decision Under Profile" .

u2:U2_0000122 skos:definition "Links an eligibility decision record to one or more u1 gate evaluation records used as evidence for the decision.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Decision Has Gate Eval" .

u2:U2_0000007 skos:definition "In layer u2 (Accepted-in-System (governance decision and promotion artefacts; append-only; supersession only)), 'Eligible' is an individual value used within this layer's governance/assurance vocabulary. It records accepted-in-system status only; it does not assert metaphysical truth and has no mechanism semantics.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligible" .

u2:U2_0000008 skos:definition "In layer u2 (Accepted-in-System (governance decision and promotion artefacts; append-only; supersession only)), 'Not Eligible' is an individual value used within this layer's governance/assurance vocabulary. It records accepted-in-system status only; it does not assert metaphysical truth and has no mechanism semantics.";
  skos:prefLabel "Not Eligible" .

u2:U2_0000123 skos:definition "Links an eligibility decision record to exactly one controlled eligibility outcome individual.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Decision Outcome" .

u2:U2_0000005 skos:definition "Binary eligibility decision for a workflow under an eligibility profile, based on explicit gate evaluations and available evidence. Governance artefact; does not imply execution.";
  skos:prefLabel "Eligibility Decision Record" .

u2:U2_0000003 skos:definition "Append-only governance record relating one prior accepted-in-system assertion to one subsequent accepted-in-system assertion.";
  skos:prefLabel "Supersession Record" .

u2:U2_0000110 skos:definition "Payload link from an append-only ledger entry to exactly one governance record (decision or supersession).";
  skos:prefLabel "Ledger Entry Has Payload" .

u2:U2_0000203 skos:definition "Monotonic sequence number for append-only ledger ordering (implementation-level discipline).";
  skos:prefLabel "Ledger Sequence" .

u2:U2_0000004 skos:definition "Append-only ledger envelope containing exactly one governance payload (one acceptance decision record or one supersession record).";
  skos:prefLabel "Append-Only Ledger Entry" .

u2:U2_0000108 skos:definition "Links a supersession record to the prior accepted-in-system assertion.";
  skos:prefLabel "Supersession Supersedes" .

u2:U2_0000109 skos:definition "Links a supersession record to the subsequent accepted-in-system assertion.";
  skos:prefLabel "Supersession Superseded By" .

u2:U2_0000202 skos:definition "Timestamp when the supersession record was issued.";
  skos:prefLabel "Supersession Time" .

<https://ontology.engender.co.za/semstack/u2> skos:definition "u2 represents accepted-in-system assertions created only by explicit governance decisions. u2 is append-only; changes occur via explicit supersession records. u2 does not assert metaphysical truth and does not encode mechanisms or workflows.";
  skos:prefLabel "Accepted-in-System Layer" .

u3:U3_0000021 skos:definition "In layer u3 (Mapping (mapped structural workflow constructs and participation; non-executive; non-governance)), 'Validation Report For Assertion' is an object property relating <https://ontology.engender.co.za/semstack/u3#U3_0000003> to <https://ontology.engender.co.za/semstack/u2#U2_0000001>. It represents mapped structure only; it does not represent execution and confers no governance authority.";
